{"line":57758,"local":"2026-10-28T18:12:02","questions":[{"question":"How should git ignore line endings across the lab from now on? Both machines already set core.autocrlf=false, core.whitespace=cr-at-eol and merge.renormalize=true. But renormalize does nothing without a text attribute, so CRLF/LF flips still conflict (reproduced in a throwaway repo).","header":"Git EOL","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Global text=auto (Recommended)","description":"Add '* text=auto' to the global git attributes file on LAB-OMARCHY (~/.config/git/attributes) and PAYTON-LEGION2 (C:\Users\kingd\.config\git\attributes); no other setting changes. Experiment result: the merge is clean, both edits kept. Effects in every repo: a file changed on both sides of a merge is committed with LF; files already committed with CRLF are otherwise left alone."},{"label":"Per-merge -Xignore-cr-at-eol","description":"No config change. Every merge I run uses -Xignore-cr-at-eol, recorded as a memory rule. Experiment result: clean, both edits kept, but a merged file can mix CRLF and LF lines. Only covers merges run with that option, not other tools or agents."}]},{"question":"Develop's new ClineQb marker contract reads CLINE_QB_PLUGIN_ROOT and CLINE_QB_PLUGIN_ARTIFACT_SHA256 straight from the process, bypassing the hermetic plugin-version sources, and its 3 tests set process variables. AC-TR-MCP-WS-005-001 already says unit tests take the agent plugin-root variables only from test-owned data. How should the merge combine them?","header":"ClineQb","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Strengthen AC, use sources (Recommended)","description":"AC-TR-MCP-WS-005-001 also names the ClineQb root and artifact-digest variables. BuildConfiguredClineQbContract reads both through the injected sources; production still reads the same process variables. Develop's 3 ClineQb tests become unit tests on test-owned sources, with every input and assertion kept. Its golden-fixture test reads a repository file, so it is tagged Integration like this branch's other repo-reading tests."},{"label":"Keep develop's tests as Integration","description":"Restore an environment save-and-restore helper for develop's 3 tests and tag them Integration (they run in the lane only); production keeps the direct read. AC-TR-MCP-WS-005-001 stays unmet: every unit test that builds the marker plugins reads CLINE_QB_PLUGIN_ROOT from the process, and ClineQb has no unit coverage."}]}],"answer":"Your questions have been answered: "How should git ignore line endings across the lab from now on? Both machines already set core.autocrlf=false, core.whitespace=cr-at-eol and merge.renormalize=true. But renormalize does nothing without a text attribute, so CRLF/LF flips still conflict (reproduced in a throwaway repo)."="Global text=auto (Recommended)", "Develop's new ClineQb marker contract reads CLINE_QB_PLUGIN_ROOT and CLINE_QB_PLUGIN_ARTIFACT_SHA256 straight from the process, bypassing the hermetic plugin-version sources, and its 3 tests set process variables. AC-TR-MCP-WS-005-001 already says unit tests take the agent plugin-root variables only from test-owned data. How should the merge combine them?"="Strengthen AC, use sources (Recommended)". You can now continue with these answers in mind.","answerLine":57759}
